.TH ZERODDS-DURABILITY-SVC.YAML 5 "" "ZeroDDS" "ZeroDDS Manual"
.SH NAME
zerodds-durability-svc.yaml \- configuration file for zerodds-durability-svc(1)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.I /etc/zerodds/durability-svc.yaml
.SH DESCRIPTION
YAML document configuring the standalone ZeroDDS Durability-Service daemon
(ADR 0009). The parser that reads it is
.IR crates/durability-service-bin/src/config.rs::DaemonConfig::from_config .
.PP
Every CLI flag of
.BR zerodds-durability-svc (1)
is a
.B --set
of the key it names below \(em
.B --domain\ N
is
.BR --set\ domain=N ,
.B --topic\ NAME
is
.BR "--set +durability.topics=NAME" .
Precedence, lowest first: compiled-in defaults, environment, this file (+ its
.I durability-svc.d/
drop-in directory), then
.BR --set .
.PP
Top-level keys:
.BR domain ", " store ", " path ", " auto ", " durability .
An unknown top-level key is a WARN line on stderr at start, and an error under
.BR --check-config ;
an unknown key
.I inside
.B durability.topics[]
stops the start (file and line).
.SH KEYS
.SS Top level
.TP
.B domain
Integer DDS domain ID. Required from some source (this file, the
environment, or
.BR --domain ).
.TP
.B store
.IR sqlite " (default) | " file " | " lakehouse " | " postgres .
.I lakehouse
and
.I postgres
need a binary built with the cargo feature of the same name.
.TP
.B path
Store location; meaning depends on
.BR store :
.IR sqlite / lakehouse ,
a database file (omitted: in-memory, lost on restart);
.IR file ,
a directory (required);
.IR postgres ,
a libpq connection string (required).
.TP
.B auto
Boolean. Auto-serve every topic whose writers declare TRANSIENT or
PERSISTENT durability \(em no application-side code needed. At least one of
.B auto
and a
.B durability.topics
entry is required (from any source, once every layer is merged).
.SS durability
.TP
.B topics
A list. Each entry is either a bare topic-name string, or a map:
.RS
.TP
.B name
Topic name. Required.
.TP
.B type
Explicit application type name. Without it, the type (and keyedness) come
from whichever writer of the topic is discovered first \(em exactly like
.B auto
does, but for a topic named explicitly and regardless of that writer's
durability kind \(em UNLESS the store already holds type/keyedness/contract
for this topic from an earlier run, in which case it resumes immediately
with no writer/reader discovered first (see
.I zerodds-durability-service
crate docs, "Resuming a served topic after a restart").
.TP
.B keyed
Boolean. Only meaningful together with
.BR type ;
without a
.BR type ,
keyedness comes from discovery (the writer's RTPS entityKind, DDSI-RTPS 2.5
\(sc9.3.1.2). With a
.B type
and no
.BR keyed ,
defaults to
.IR false .
.TP
.B contract
Sub-map pinning the retention contract regardless of what a discovered
writer's own
.B DurabilityServiceQosPolicy
(DDS 1.4 \(sc2.2.3.5) announces. Fields:
.BR history_kind " (" keep_last " | " keep_all "), " history_depth ,
.BR max_samples ", " max_instances ", " max_samples_per_instance
(integers, \-1 = unlimited), and
.B cleanup_delay_secs
(integer seconds \(em the grace period after an instance is
disposed/unregistered before its samples are purged). A field left out keeps
.BR keep_all 's
unlimited value for it, not the DDS policy default of
.IR KEEP_LAST(1) .
.RE
.SH WHICH CONTRACT WINS
Per topic, in order: this file's
.B contract
override; else what the store already has persisted for this topic from an
earlier run (see
.B type ,
above); else the discovered writer's own
.B DurabilityServiceQosPolicy
(whenever it differs from the DDS default, which is indistinguishable on the
wire from "never touched"); else this daemon's own default
(.BR KEEP_ALL ,
passed to
.B enable_auto_discovery
/
.B serve_discovered
internally).
.PP
Two writers of one topic that announce
.I different
.B DurabilityServiceQosPolicy
values: the daemon applies the
.I first
discovered writer's contract for the topic's lifetime and reports the
disagreement (never silently switches retention policy on a store that
already holds data under the old one) \(em see the
.I zerodds-durability-service
crate docs, "Two writers, one topic". The same rule covers a writer whose
announced type name or keyedness disagrees with what the topic is already
served under (from stored metadata or an earlier writer): reported, not
applied.
.SH EXAMPLE
.nf
domain: 0
store: sqlite
auto: true
durability:
  topics:
    - Sensors
    - name: Commands
      type: demo::Command
      keyed: true
      contract:
        history_kind: keep_last
        history_depth: 5
        max_instances: 1000
        cleanup_delay_secs: 300
.fi
.SH FILES
.I /etc/zerodds/durability-svc.yaml.example
Shipped, commented example \(em loaded back by a unit test
(.IR crates/durability-service-bin/src/config.rs ),
so it never drifts from what the parser accepts.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR zerodds-durability-svc (1)
.SH AUTHOR
ZeroDDS Contributors
